NOVEMBER 3 AMENDMENT TO OCTOBER 26th AMENDMENT BY SUBSTITUTE

ORDINANCE NO.__________
ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTERS 10.44, WEIGHT LIMITS,
WITHIN TITLE 10, VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC, OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING.”
BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:
Section 1. That sections of Chapter 10.44, Weight Limits, of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, is
hereby amended as set out in this Ordinance. Sections currently existing in Chapter 10.44 not set
out within this ordinance remain unchanged.
10.44.010 - Commercial motor carrier vehicle defined.
Unless the context of this chapter otherwise requires, the term "commercial motor carrier
vehicle", when used in this chapter shall be construed to mean any truck, trailer or combination
thereof, carrying or constructed to carry cargo other than personnel, for gain or for profit, and
having a rated load capacity gross vehicle weight of ten thousand and one (10,001) pounds
one ton or more., for hire.
10.44.020 - Purpose.
The prevention of unnecessary wear and tear on the streets of the city and the elimination of
unnecessary traffic hazards and loss of life and property resulting from such traffic hazards,
caused by the unregulated and unrestricted use of the streets of the city by certain types of motor
vehicles, and the maintenance of a sound, well-regulated traffic system for the people of the city
are declared to be the objectives of this chapter, and the provisions of this chapter are the means
to that end. In order to align the purpose and enforcement of this section, any revenue generated
to the city from enforcement shall be directed by the City Treasurer to road maintenance or
construction.
10.44.030 - Applicability.
The terms of this chapter shall not be construed to apply to any motor vehicle operating
exclusively within the city and carrying cargo from place to place within the limits of the city
and its immediate environs.
10.44.040 - Load Thru truck restrictions upon vehicles using certain highways.
When signs are erected giving notice thereof, no person No commercial motor carrier shall
operate any vehicle with a gross vehicle weight in excess of the amounts specified in Schedule
H, attached to the ordinance codified in this section and made a part hereof, at any time upon any
By Joe Chenchar at 2:35 pm, Nov 06, 2020
```

### Page 2 of 5

```text
of the streets or parts of streets described in Schedule H without a scheduled stop in such
locality.
Schedule H is adopted by reference and is on file in the offices of the city clerk, traffic engineer
and police department.
Roads identified in Schedule H shall be identified by the black and white regulatory sign:

10.44.050 - Truck routes.
In order to expedite the movement of commercial motor carrier vehicle traffic within and
through the city and to eliminate the traffic hazards and obstructions resulting from the
unrestricted use of the streets of the city by such motor carriers, the streets listed in Schedule I,
attached to the ordinance codified in this section and made a part hereof, are established and
designated "truck routes," to be used by commercial motor carriers vehicles when passing
through the city in the directions indicated.
Schedule I is adopted by reference and is on file in the offices of the city clerk, traffic engineer
and police department.
10.44.060 – Authority to weigh and measure.
The chief of police, or his designee, shall have the authority to require the driver of any vehicle
operating on the streets of the city, and which he has reason to believe is overweight or oversize,
to proceed with the vehicle to an appropriate weight station or stopping place for the purpose of
determining whether this chapter has been complied with.
The chief of police, or designee measuring vehicle size and weight shall use calibrated scales and
be certified in the use of such scales and measurements.
10.44.70 – Height, width, weight and traffic control escorts – Permit conditions.
A. No vehicle, unladen or with load or load-holding devices thereon, in excess of one
hundred two (102) inches wide, fourteen (14) feet high, or eighty-five (85) feet in length,
single or in combination, shall be driven upon any city street without a permit provided
by the traffic engineer.
B. Any vehicle over twenty thousand (20,000) pounds on one axle, thirty-six thousand
(36,000) pounds on tandem axles, forty-two thousand (42,000) pounds on tri-axles and
any vehicle over eighty thousand (80,0000) one hundred seventeen thousand (117,000)
pounds is overweight and shall not be driven upon any city street without a permit
provided by the traffic engineer.
