```text
C. Public safety vehicles, such as fire apparatus, snow plowing equipment, police rescue
vehicles, tow trucks, and vehicles used in emergency infrastructure repair are exempt
from this section.
10.44.80 – Permit Application.
A. A person may operate a vehicle with a gross vehicle weight in excess of the amounts
specified in Schedule H and 10.44.070, and/or a height or width in excess of the amounts
specified in 10.44.070, by receiving a special permit for operation of oversize and
overweight loads on City of Cheyenne roads.
B. Permit applications shall be filed with the traffic engineer within the time specified by the
permit application unless there is an emergency.
C. Emergencies shall be approved by the traffic engineer on a case-by-case basis and require
a permit to be obtained after the fact.
D. The traffic engineer shall be permitted to create permit applications in conformity with
the requirements of Wyoming State Statute and this Chapter. The requirements of such
permits shall be approved by resolution of the governing body.
E. Permit applicants must agree to obey all state laws and ordinances of the city of
Cheyenne.
F. Issuance of a permit shall not relieve the holder or their assigns acting on the holder’s
behalf from responsibility for damages to any roadways or structures or other
appurtenances.
G. F. (Strike letter G replace with F) At the direction of the traffic engineer, police or private
escorts may be required for traffic control.
10.44.90 – Permit Fee Schedule
A. For oversize vehicles, in accordance with Section 10.44.070(A), the permit fee shall be
established by resolution of the governing body on recommendation of the city engineer
on any load that is in excess of one hundred two (102) inches wide, fourteen (14) feet
high, or eighty-five (85) feet in length, single or in the combination.
B. For overweight vehicles, in accordance with Section 10.44.070(B) and/or Schedule H, the
fee shall be established by resolution of the governing body on recommendation of the
city engineer the city engineer on any load that is in exceeds the amounts specified in
Section 10.44.070(B) and/or Schedule H.
C. Any additional costs of police escorts and other related traffic control fees shall be
assessed by the traffic engineer and chief of police.
D. All remedial permits issued after the oversize or overweight load was moved will be
assessed an additional two-hundred-fifty-dollar ($250.00) fee per load in addition to
original permit fees if the load cannot be divided to meet legal standards.
10.44.100 – Permitted operation on non-truck-route streets.
The operation of commercial motor carriers vehicle over and along any city street not designated
a truck route, shall be permitted only for the purpose of reaching a point of destination inside the
city, provided that:
```

### Page 4 of 5

```text
A. One Destination Point. All commercial motor carriers vehicles having a single destination
point in the city shall proceed only over an established truck route and shall deviate only
at the intersection with the street upon which such traffic is permitted nearest to the
destination point. A deviating commercial motor carrier vehicle shall return to the truck
route by the shortest possible route;
B. Multiple Destination Points. All commercial motor carriers vehicles having multiple
destination points shall proceed only over established truck routes and shall deviate only
at the intersection with the street upon which such traffic is permitted, nearest to the first
destination point. Upon leaving the first destination point, a deviating commercial motor
carrier vehicle shall return to the nearest truck route and proceed to other destination
points by the shortest direction, and only over streets upon which such traffic is
permitted. Upon leaving the last destination point, a deviating commercial motor carrier
vehicle shall return to the truck route by the shortest permissible route.
C. Routes for Construction as Designated by the Traffic Engineer. If Tthe traffic engineer
may appoints a truck route as part of a construction site plans or construction
activities.information shall be included in the design plans and specifications prior to the
project being put out to bid.
10.44.110 – Operation of tracked vehicles – prohibited on city streets.
No person shall operate any vehicle equipped with continuous tracks, at any time, upon any of
the streets or parts of streets within the city of Cheyenne.
10.44.120 – Bypass of port of entry – prohibited.
No commercial vehicle shall bypass any port of entry by using city streets within the city of
Cheyenne.
10.44.130 – Violation – Penalty
It is unlawful for any person to operate or cause to be operated any vehicle within the city in
violation of this chapter. Violations of this chapter are punishable in accordance with the general
penalty provisions of Chapter 1.24 of the Cheyenne Municipal Code.
Section 2. That Section 10.44.040, Load restrictions upon vehicles using certain highways, of
Chapter 10.44, Weight Limits, within Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne, is hereby amended to adopt that amended Schedule H attached to this
Ordinance as Exhibit A.
Section 3. That Section 10.44.050, Truck routes, of Chapter 10.44, Weight Limits, within Title
10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, is hereby amended to
adopt that amended Schedule I attached to this Ordinance as Exhibit B.
Section 4. This ordinance shall be in full force and effect on April 1, 2021.
```

